'''Orient Paper Mill''' is a [[paper]] and paper crafts manufacturer in [[Amlai]] ([[Madhya Pradesh]]), [[India]]. It has been associated with paper manufacture in [[Africa]].<ref>[http://www.ckbirlagroup.com/orient-paper.php CK Birla Group, Orient Paper]</ref> The mill is part of Orient Paper & Industries which comprises the paper facility and manufacturers of [[Portland cement]] and [[ceiling fan]]s, and which itself is a subsidiary of [[CK Birla Group]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.ckbirlagroup.com/group-profile.php|title=Group Profile {{!}} CK Birla Group|website=www.ckbirlagroup.com|access-date=2018-10-25|archive-date=24 April 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180424202614/http://www.ckbirlagroup.com/group-profile.php|url-status=live}}</ref>

Orient has worked with Pan African Paper Mills in [[Kenya]], in partnership with the [[Government of Kenya]] and the [[International Finance Corporation]].

The Orient Paper Mill was awarded the Golden Peacock Environment Management Award for 2006 by the World Environment Foundation (WEF).<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.agencyfaqs.com/news/company_news/Corporate/8750.html |title=agencyfaqs, article 'Orient Paper Mills declared the winner of "Golden Peacock Environment Management Award' |access-date=10 June 2007 |archive-date=27 September 2007 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070927045553/http://www.agencyfaqs.com/news/company_news/Corporate/8750.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

